+{"parentUuid":"06cb9e3c-1f6b-496d-b976-4428f6cf9f77","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"beec94bb-07ed-4444-9ea6-49797267a66e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n\n   Write `approach.py` with class `GeneratedApproach(action_space, observation_space, primitives)` having `reset(state, info)` and `get_action(state)` methods, for the black-box \"Rovers\" env (PDDLStream rovers).\n   - **Goal:** one stone and one soil analysis plus every objective imaged, all received by the lander, both rovers back home, both stores empty.\n   - **Scoring:** reward is -1 per step, so minimise steps. Each instance gets 60s wall-clock.\n   - **Imports:** only stdlib, numpy, scipy and sibling files. No importlib/runpy/`__import__`/sys.modules. approach.py must NOT import env_client.\n   - **Files:** write everything with relative paths in /sandbox.\n   - **Git:** commit often with `git add -A && git commit -m ...`, committing before testing. Commit messages end with \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\".\n   - **Python:** use /opt/robocode-strict/bin/python.\n   - **Context management:** delegate heavy reading to subagents and keep outputs short (pipe through head/tail).\n   - **MCP tools** (render_state, render_policy) must be called directly by me, never inside subagents.\n   - **Process:** keep approach.py as the best current attempt at all times, then search for failing instances and improve.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts (empirically found)**\n\n   **Fixed layout** (same in every episode):\n   - Rover0 starts at (1,-1.75) with θ=π; rover1 at (-1,-1.75) with θ=0.\n   - Lander at (-1.9,-2.0).\n   - Mounds `obstacle0`–`3` at (2,2), (-2,2), (0.5,2), (-0.5,2), half 0.25, half_z 0.05.\n\n   **Random per episode:** 1–3 objectives on the mounds, 8 pillars (half 0.05, half_z 0.2), and 6 samples (3 stone, then 3 soil).\n\n   **Hidden wall:**\n   - Sits at x=0 and has no gap.\n   - Rover centre limits: |x| ≥ 0.227, |x|,|y| ≤ 2.273.\n   - Blocks motion only, not line of sight.\n\n   **Motion:**\n   - dx/dy are in the world frame and applied exactly, clipped to ±0.2.\n   - Theta wraps to [-π, π].\n   - A colliding move is rejected entirely (no sliding).\n   - Footprint: about a circle of 0.177 against mounds.\n   - Against pillars the footprint is box-like and turns with heading: gap to pillar face about 0.196 ahead and 0.183 at sides/back.\n   - Lander contact at about 0.69–0.73 from its centre.\n\n   **Operators:** each operator is evaluated on the POST-motion pose, so an operator can share a step with motion.\n\n   **Camera point:** `cam = (x,y) + R(θ)·(-0.087, -0.0125)`.\n\n   **Operator preconditions:**\n\n   | Operator | Precondition / behaviour |\n   |---|---|\n   | calibrate | Some objective within 2D 1.9976 of `cam`, with line of sight clear of pillars. Heading only matters through the camera offset. |\n   | image | Requires calibrated; photographs the nearest visible objective this rover hasn't imaged yet (even if another rover already sent it); consumes calibration. |\n   | send | Lander within about 3.989 of `cam`. Blocked by pillars (narrow shadow) and by the other rover. Sends everything the rover holds. |\n   | sample | Rover centre within 0.250 of a sample and store empty. Analyses the nearest sample in range. Samples never disappear. |\n   | drop | Clears the store. |\n\n   **Selector values:** sample=-5/6, calibrate=-0.5, image=-1/6, noop=0, send=0.5, drop=5/6.\n\n   **Episode end:** the env sets terminated=True when the goal completes. max_steps is 1000.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n\n   **approach.py** — the main file, roughly 750 lines.\n\n   *Constants:*\n   - RES=0.05, CELLS_PER_STEP=4, NI=41, NJ=91.\n   - OBJ_RANGE=1.97, OBJ_RANGE_EXEC=1.99.\n   - LANDER_RANGE=3.95, LANDER_RANGE_EXEC=3.975.\n   - SAMPLE_RANGE=0.24, SAMPLE_RANGE_EXEC=0.245.\n   - HOME_RANGE=0.15, IMG_PEN=1.0.\n   - PILLAR_INFL_X=0.21, PILLAR_INFL_Y=0.20 (box model via `_pillar_free`).\n   - MOUND_INFL=0.20, LANDER_CLEAR=0.78, ROVER_BLOCK_R=0.22.\n   - CAM_OFF=(-0.087,-0.0125).\n\n   *Helpers:* `_box_dist`, `_seg_box_hit` (slab test), `_seg_circle_hit`, `_pillar_free(px,py,ox,oy,hx,hy,slack)`.\n\n   *`Side` class:* one grid per rover half (x = sign·(0.25+0.05i), y = -2.25+0.05j).\n   - Holds the free mask, camera-point arrays CX/CY, and an 8-connected graph with unit edges.\n   - `field_from(init)` runs a multi-source Dijkstra with initial offsets through a super-source node, adding +1 to edge weights and subtracting it afterwards.\n   - `dist_from_node` is cached.\n   - Also has `node_of`, `pos` and `cell_of`.\n   - Headings are kept fixed at the home heading.\n\n   *`reset`:* parses static objects (pillars have half_z > 0.1) and builds the `Side`s. It then builds regions per rover:\n   - (\"O\",k): within OBJ_RANGE, line of sight clear with pillar margin 0.03. Also stores `ovis`/`odist` for the loose visibility used by `_img_mask`.\n   - (\"S\"/\"T\",k): within SAMPLE_RANGE, and the target must be strictly the nearest sample (others farther than dk+0.02).\n   - \"send\": within LANDER_RANGE, line of sight clear with margin 0.03, and not shadowed by the other rover's home (radius ROVER_BLOCK_R+0.05).\n   - \"home\": radius HOME_RANGE. In the current uncommitted variant this is 0.01 for the rover nearer the lander, otherwise HOME_RANGE.\n   - Finally calls `_make_plan`, then initialises blacklist, stuck, targets, last_pos, `_bw_cache`, forced, bad_points, cmd and `_pred`.\n\n   *Planner:*\n   - `_img_mask(rn,k,imaged)` excludes cells where a non-imaged objective other than k is visible and closer.\n   - `_rover_costs` does a DFS over task sequences using layered `field_from`, with at most one stone and one soil per rover. Cost = min(F + send-to-home)/4 + IMG_PEN·n_img + 1, subject to a deadline.\n   - `_make_plan` enumerates objective assignments × stone choice × soil choice, assigning each sample to the rover whose side has it. It minimises (max, sum) and stores `self.plan` (an ordered task list per rover) and `plan_score`.\n\n   *Execution:*\n   - `_remaining` gives undone plan tasks, then \"send\" if needed (or if unsent data remains), then \"home\".\n   - `_backward` computes cost-to-go fields for the remaining sequence (cached).\n   - `_target` chooses argmin of dist(cur,·) + G[0] within the task mask. For send it excludes cells whose line of sight is blocked by the other rover's predicted position at arrival time (karr = max(ceil(d/4),1), indexed into the `_pred` trajectory). Blacklisted cells are excluded.\n   - `_next_pos` follows the descent path up to 12 cells and picks the furthest cell within Chebyshev 0.2 that passes `_seg_free`. Its fallback is the first path cell unless that is a bad point.\n   - `_seg_free` checks the endpoint strictly (slack 0.01) and intermediate points with slack 0.05. `_point_free` also rejects bad_points.\n   - Rejected moves are recorded in `bad_points`.\n   - Stuck detection blacklists the target cell after more than 2 stuck steps.\n   - `_lookahead`: for image/send tasks, tries to perform the op while moving toward rem[1:]. Image fires if already calibrated; calibrate fires at p1 if p2 still sees k as the nearest needed objective; send fires if the lander is visible at p1.\n   - `_choose_op` priority:\n     1. sample (nearest in range and of a needed type)\n     2. image (calibrated, and the nearest needed visible objective is mine — or any of mine if stuck ≥ 2)\n     3. drop, if a sample type is still needed\n     4. calibrate\n     5. send\n     6. drop\n     7. noop\n   - `get_action` predicts both rovers' trajectories (up to 25 steps toward their previous targets), computes motion targets, applies forced ops, steers heading back to the home heading, and records cmd.\n\n   **test_approach.py:** runs seeds given as a comma list and prints per seed: n, steps, done, plan score, tplan, ttot, plan; ends with \"total X fails [...]\".\n\n   **trace.py `<seed> <n>`:** per-step trace of ops, targets, rover states, and objective/sample flags.\n\n   **stats.py:** idle and rejected-move counts per rover.\n\n   **Probe scripts** (probe_motion.py, probe_vis.py, survey.py, t_order.py, dbg.py) and **result files** (res*.txt, big*_*.txt) are also present.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n\n   - **Seed 43 stuck:** image targeted the wrong objective (nearest-needed rule). Fixed with order-aware `_img_mask`, an image-anyway fallback, and `_unsent` restricted to unreceived types.\n   - **Trace script bug:** the stale `g = obs.get` binding was fixed by re-binding after each step.\n   - **Send waiting while the other rover blocks line of sight:** fixed by backward cost-to-go targeting each step, exclusion of blocked send cells, and predicted-trajectory blocking. Two follow-up fixes:\n     - The mask slice bug (trajectory of length 1).\n     - The off-by-one (karr ≥ 1).\n   - **Seed 5 diagonal move rejected near a pillar corner:** fixed with the box-footprint pillar model, recording of rejected moves, a lenient segment check, and a one-cell fallback.\n   - **Ranges too conservative:** tightened, which brought the total from 1378 to 1361.\n   - **Seed 117 (45 steps):** a closer stone sample stole the soil sample op. Fixed by requiring the target sample to be the nearest one in the region (117 → 25 steps, 116 → 22).\n   - **Experiments with no gain:** tighter obstacle inflation and HOME_RANGE 0.22 (both reverted), and IMG_PEN 0.5/0.0 (kept 1.0).\n\n5. **Problem Solving / Results**\n\n   - All seeds 0–259 are solved, with at most about 3.7s per episode.\n   - Seeds 0–59 total progression: 2696 → 1482 → 1384 → 1378 → 1361 → 1352 (with lookahead).\n   - Plan estimates match actual totals closely.\n   - The critical rover usually idles 1–2 steps.\n   - Remaining inefficiency is mainly the other rover blocking send line of sight at the end, and inherent long routes.\n   - Latest comparison on seeds 60–259: the variant with an exact home target for the rover nearer the lander scored 4496, versus 4505 for the base (HOME_RANGE 0.15 for both). On seeds 0–59 the variant scored 1354 versus 1352.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n\n   - The only user message was the initial task description, summarised in section 1. It included the instructions: write all files with relative paths in /sandbox; never import env_client in approach.py; allowed imports are only stdlib, numpy, scipy and sibling files; commit often; MCP tools can't be called from subagents; use /opt/robocode-strict/bin/python.\n   - CLAUDE.md adds: delegate source reading to subagents, keep thinking brief, and pipe output through head/tail.\n   - There was no further user feedback.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n\n   - Keep improving step efficiency.\n   - Search for failing or slow instances.\n   - Keep approach.py committed as the best version.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n\n   The A/B test just finished: \"variant 4496, base 4505\". After `git stash pop`, approach.py holds the uncommitted variant. The variant changed the home region in `reset` to:\n\n   ```python\n   dl = math.hypot(hxy[0] - self.lander[0], hxy[1] - self.lander[1])\n   dlo = math.hypot(oh[0] - self.lander[0], oh[1] - self.lander[1])\n   hr = 0.01 if dl < dlo else HOME_RANGE\n   reg[\"home\"] = np.hypot(px - hxy[0], py - hxy[1]) <= hr\n   ```\n\n   This was the last change I tested; the variant was better on the 200-seed set.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n\n   - Commit the variant: `git add -A && git commit -m \"Exact home target for rover nearer lander (reduces send LOS blocking)\"`, verifying first that `git diff` shows only this change.\n   - Continue searching for slow seeds by sorting the actual-minus-plan gap in bigB_*.txt.\n   - Possibly render a policy run via MCP for a visual sanity check.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-sandbox/2bdabd45-4dd3-4ae3-a755-e3071de60b54.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"7754a44b-e82a-412a-aabd-91f2663aad68","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:32:42.752Z","turnOrigin":"sdk","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/sandbox","sessionId":"2bdabd45-4dd3-4ae3-a755-e3071de60b54","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"master","slug":"purring-baking-crystal"}
